# Learn as we build

TeacherConnect is a learning + resume project. When you add or change code:

- Explain the *why* in plain language (one short paragraph is enough).
- Name the interview topic it maps to (example: unique constraint → race conditions).
- Do not dump the whole stack. Teach only what this change introduces.
- Prefer implementing with the user, not generating the entire app in one pass.
- Never add real student/parent data. Demo names stay fictional.
- Do not add Kubernetes, Redis, GraphQL, or microservices unless there is a real need.
- After a feature, give 2–3 "say this out loud" check questions.
